Assigning the predefined global MYUSERNAME or a STARLIMS status keyword
(Pending) silently changes what every later reader sees
(diag.global_assignment). Reads and comparisons of the same names do not
fire.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE ImpersonateRunner;
	:PARAMETERS sRunner;
	:DECLARE sPrevious, bIsPending, sStatus;
	sPrevious := MYUSERNAME;
	MYUSERNAME := sRunner;
	Pending := "Waiting";
	bIsPending := sStatus == Pending;
	MYUSERNAME := sPrevious;
	:RETURN bIsPending;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE ImpersonateRunner;
	:PARAMETERS sRunner;
	:DECLARE sPrevious, bIsPending, sStatus;
	sPrevious := MYUSERNAME;
	MYUSERNAME := sRunner;
	Pending := "Waiting";
	bIsPending := sStatus == Pending;
	MYUSERNAME := sPrevious;
	:RETURN bIsPending;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
5:2-5:12 warning global_assignment: Assignment to global variable 'MYUSERNAME' changes it for every routine that reads it
6:2-6:9 warning global_assignment: Assignment to global variable 'Pending' changes it for every routine that reads it
8:2-8:12 warning global_assignment: Assignment to global variable 'MYUSERNAME' changes it for every routine that reads it
